{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>But the field, when it goes out in the Jubilee.</b> From the hand of the one who bought it from the treasurer — like the way of other fields that go out from the hand of their buyers in the Jubilee." "<b>Holy to YHWH.</b> Not that it returns to be consecrated for the Temple repair, to the hand of the treasurer, but <b>like a devoted field</b> given to the priests — as it says ״כָּל חֵרֶם בְּיִשְׂרָאֵל לְךָ יִהְיֶה״ (Numbers 18) — so too this is divided among the priests of the watch on which the Day of Atonement of the Jubilee falls (Arakhin 28)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:58.525455771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}